# Trivy HIGH/CRITICAL suppressions for the docker workflow's image scan.
# Mirrors the backend pip-audit allowlist convention: every entry is a
# deliberate, documented acceptance — not a blanket mute. `ignore-unfixed`
# is already on in docker.yml, so everything here HAS a fix available but
# is being consciously deferred with a stated reason.
#
# Review rule: anything reachable from the *runtime* attack surface gets
# upgraded, not ignored. The entries below are all build/dev tooling that
# only lands in the image because frontend/Dockerfile is a dev container
# (`npm ci` installs devDependencies, CMD is `npm run dev`). They are not
# part of the served Next.js runtime an external client can reach.
#
# Proper fix (logged as tech debt, skills.md): give the frontend a
# multi-stage production Dockerfile (`next build` + standalone output, no
# devDependencies) so this whole class of dev-toolchain CVEs stops landing
# in the scanned image. Once that exists, delete this file.

# --- frontend dev-toolchain transitives (node_modules build tools) ---
# (rollup's CVE-2026-27606 is NOT listed here — it's actually fixed via a
# package.json `overrides` pin to rollup 3.30.0, not suppressed.)

# cross-spawn ReDoS — dev tooling path parsing, not request-path.
CVE-2024-21538

# glob CLI command injection — only via the glob binary's CLI, which we
# never invoke; it's a transitive lib dep of build tooling.
CVE-2025-64756

# minimatch ReDoS / unbounded-recursion DoS — glob-pattern matching in
# build tooling, fed static patterns, not attacker input.
CVE-2026-26996
CVE-2026-27903
CVE-2026-27904

# node-tar path-traversal / arbitrary-file-write on EXTRACTION. Fixes only
# exist in tar 7.x (major bump of an npm-internal transitive). We never
# extract untrusted archives at runtime — tar is pulled in by install-time
# tooling that unpacks our own trusted, lockfile-pinned packages.
CVE-2026-23745
CVE-2026-23950
CVE-2026-24842
CVE-2026-26960
CVE-2026-29786
CVE-2026-31802

# vitest UI-server arbitrary-file-read. Fix is vitest 4.x (major bump from
# the 2.1.x we pin). The vulnerable surface is the `vitest --ui` dev server,
# which we never start — vitest runs headless in CI/local and ships only
# because the dev container installs devDependencies.
CVE-2026-47429

# --- esbuild Go binary: stdlib CVEs from its compiled-in Go runtime ---
# `@esbuild/*/bin/esbuild` is a Go binary built with Go 1.20.12, so Trivy's
# gobinary scanner flags every net/http, crypto, archive, etc. stdlib CVE in
# that Go release. esbuild is a build-time bundler (transitive of vite/
# vitest); it is never invoked by, nor reachable from, the served Next.js
# runtime. Bumping its embedded Go means bumping esbuild itself, which is
# pinned transitively — deferred to the multi-stage prod-Dockerfile fix that
# drops devDependencies from the image entirely (see header).
CVE-2023-45288
CVE-2024-24790
CVE-2024-34156
CVE-2025-61726
CVE-2025-61729
CVE-2025-68121
CVE-2026-25679
CVE-2026-27142
CVE-2026-32280
CVE-2026-32281
CVE-2026-32283
CVE-2026-33811
CVE-2026-33814
CVE-2026-39820
CVE-2026-39823
CVE-2026-39825
CVE-2026-39826
CVE-2026-39836
CVE-2026-42499
